times seems to wipe them clean enough to work.
I doubt there is enough clearance to get even
a thin q-tip into it to wipe a bit of vaseline
across the contacts.  But, I can appreciate the
vaseline approach... I have been using that on
WWII era radio equipment, for years.  And no,
no pencil eraser cleaning of computer bits....
(:+}}...

My guess for a possible cleaning tool would be
a thin putty knife about 2 inches wide, with
a piece of soft cotton T-shirt taped to it and
then dipped into some isopropyl and inserted
into the connector....

Bob


