> The PMAG-B card is in TC0 slot of the 3 slots.
>
> Is there something I am doing wrong or need to
> twiddle?

NetBSD calls PMAG-B TC framebuffer option card "cfb"   Did
you uncomment two "cfb" lines in TCWSCONS?

> I was under the impression that the video card
> needed to go in the lowest numbered slot (0).
> Is this correct?

When multiple TC framebuffers are installed, the one which sits in
lowest numbered slot is chosen as system console, not in slot 0.

PMAGB-A (HX) or any of PXG cards is highly recommended for
the video rendering performance reason.

Toru Nishimura/ALKYL Technology



