Hello Jens

On 25-Dez-02, you wrote:
> What does one need to run netscape?

Not much: just go to /usr/pkgsrc/emulators/osf1_lib/ and type "make install"
to get the Tru64-compatibilty-package. Remember that you need to have
option COMPAT_OSF1 set in your Kernel.
Then enter /usr/pkgsrc/www/communicator and type "make install".

Communicator 4.78 runs very smooth on my Flamingo+, but I have a strange
DNS-Problem: It only opens connections to hosts I entered in /etc/hosts by
hand. Not a very useful way to access WWW-pages. :( How can I solve this
resolve-problem?

btw: Mozilla 1.2.1 _is_ a bit too big. It runs at about 1/100th the speed of
the old Communicator. I'd call this "unusable", even with the latest
-current-Kernel 1.6K.

Regards,
